    "title": "Suspect in Pepper Pike road rage incident arrested - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Justin Dennis ,\n10 hours ago\nWatch the video above for previous coverage.\nPEPPER PIKE , Ohio (WJW) — The suspect in a January road rage incident in Pepper Pike has been arrested and is now free on bond.\nSurveillance video previously released by Pepper Pike police shows a driver getting out of his car then punching and kicking another driver’s car door Jan. 13 at the intersection of Brainard and Cedar roads.\nVIDEO: Greyhound bus catches fire on I-71 South in Cleveland The victim told police an unknown man had followed him from Interstate 480 East to Interstate 271 North. Surveillance video shows the alleged attacker even followed the victim as he made a U-turn.\nThey then pulled to a stop at a red light at the Brainard-Cedar intersection and the alleged attacker got out and slammed his elbow into the other car’s window then kicked its door.\nIt was caught on another driver’s vehicle camera system, according to police.\nTwo charged in Canton home explosion Steven G. Mills, 49, of Cleveland, is now facing charges of criminal damaging, menacing and disorderly conduct in Shaker Heights Municipal Court, to which he pleaded not guilty this week, records show.\nU.S. Marshals , who named Mills their “Fugitive of the Week” last month, arrested him on Wednesday, July 29.\nMills is now free after posting 10% of a $7,500 bond following his arraignment.\nNo future court dates have been set.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to Fox 8 Cleveland WJW.\n6",
    "summary": "Surveillance video shows the alleged attacker even followed the victim as he made a U-turn. They then pulled to a stop at a red light at the Brainard-Cedar intersection and the alleged attacker got out and slammed his elbow into the other car’s window then kicked its door. Two charged in Canton home explosion Steven G. Mills, 49, of Cleveland, is now facing charges of criminal damaging, menacing and disorderly conduct in Shaker Heights Municipal Court, to which he pleaded not guilty this week, records show.",
